WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.570
On the coast of Victoria,
in south-east Australia,

2
00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:07.990
limestone stacks called the
Twelve Apostles rise from the sea.

3
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.130
Southern Ocean swells strike
with the full force of the ocean,

4
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.950
and the rock is relatively soft.

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.430
In 1990, London Bridge's arch collapsed,
stranding two visitors on the new island

6
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:22.070
until a helicopter rescued them.

7
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.740
Millions of people come
to see these towers.

8
00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.830
So should anyone try to stop the sea?

9
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.270
With sea walls?

10
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.890
In this mission, you'll see what
makes this coast so high-energy,

11
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.450
and how its landforms are linked.

12
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:40.670
Then you'll track change on this coast,
from a few seconds to thousands of years.

13
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:45.050
Your mission: decide whether anyone
should try to stop the sea wrecking these

14
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.110
rock towers.
